PREFIX app: <did:ng:z:cairns/>
PREFIX schema: <https://schema.org/>
PREFIX dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>
PREFIX prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#>
PREFIX xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>

# A recommendation (Specs §4.1): "Ana told me about this in March", not "I plan
# to go here". Provenance first, which is what keeps it in a memory app.
#
# Unlike every other object the app owns, these do not get a document each: they
# are subjects inside one list document (§3.7), addressed by fragment, exactly
# as an unnamed location is a subject inside its memory. Spike 7 established
# that the ORM reads such subjects over the wildcard scope; spike 10 established
# that it also notices new ones appearing in a document it is already watching.
#
# EXTRA a: an item asserts both app:Recommendation and schema:ListItem, for the
# same reason a memory asserts schema:Event — legibility to an application that
# has never heard of Cairns.
app:RecommendationShape EXTRA a {
  a [app:Recommendation] ;
  # The referent: a place or an event (§4.2). A reference, never nested — the
  # thing recommended has identity of its own, or it is not recommendable.
  schema:item IRI ;
  # Who told you, as a contact.
  prov:wasAttributedTo IRI ? ;
  # Who told you, when they are not a contact: a URL or free text (§4.1). Held
  # as a string in both cases rather than as an IRI-or-literal union, which
  # spike 7 showed the ORM cannot read back; the app links it when it parses as
  # a URL. One property, one datatype, and no information lost.
  dcterms:source xsd:string ? ;
  # When you were told — precision-aware (§3.1), and optional, because "Ana
  # mentioned this at some point" is a complete record.
  dcterms:date xsd:dateTime OR xsd:date OR xsd:gYearMonth OR xsd:gYear ? ;
  # What they said about it.
  schema:description xsd:string ? ;
  dcterms:subject IRI * ;
  # No "fulfilled" property. A recommendation is fulfilled when a memory points
  # at it with prov:wasInfluencedBy (§4.1) — derived, never stored, and written
  # in the memory's own document rather than into this shared list.
}
